This gives you a clean architecture:
	☐ 1. Parse the module and collect its imports.
	☐ 2. Resolve imported symbols to their actual module exports.
	☐ 3. Identify compile-time operations and their callbacks.
	☐ 4. Execute those callbacks in the compile-time environment.
	☐ 5. Apply generated code or transformations to the compilation graph.
	☐ 6. Run semantic analysis and type-check the resulting program.